The following line is parameterized, so that its direction vector is of the form $\begin{pmatrix} -7 \\ b \end{pmatrix}.$  Find $b.$

[asy]
unitsize(0.4 cm);

pair A, B, L, R;
int i, n;

for (i = -8; i <= 8; ++i) {
  draw((i,-8)--(i,8),gray(0.7));
  draw((-8,i)--(8,i),gray(0.7));
}

draw((-8,0)--(8,0),Arrows(6));
draw((0,-8)--(0,8),Arrows(6));

A = (-5,4);
B = (-1,3);
L = extension(A, B, (-8,0), (-8,1));
R = extension(A, B, (8,0), (8,1));

draw(L--R, red);

label("$x$", (8,0), E);
label("$y$", (0,8), N);
[/asy]

Let $z = 2 + \sqrt{2} - (3 + 3 \sqrt{2})i$, and let $c = 2 - 3i$.  Let $w$ be the result when $z$ is rotated around $c$ by $\frac{\pi}{4}$ counter-clockwise.

[asy]
unitsize(0.6 cm);

pair C, W, Z;

Z = (2 + sqrt(2), -3 - 3*sqrt(2));
C = (2,-3);
W = rotate(45,C)*(Z);

draw(Z--C--W);

dot("$c$", C, N);
dot("$w$", W, SE);
dot("$z$", Z, S);
label("$\frac{\pi}{4}$", C + (0.6,-1));
[/asy]

Find $w.$

3. How many distinct sums can be made from adding together exactly 8 numbers that are chosen
from the set {1, 4, 7, 10}, where each number in the set is chosen at least once? (For example,
one possible sum is 1 + 1 + 1 + 4 + 7 + 7 + 10 + 10 = 41.)
